# User-uploaded content — lives only on the server, never in the repo, so a
# future `git add -A` can't accidentally start tracking it (and risk a later
# deploy's "reset to last commit" discarding uploads made after that commit).
# The shared assets/uploads/.htaccess (blocking PHP execution) stays tracked.
assets/uploads/jobs/
assets/uploads/companies/
